// ==== src/paint/layer.js
// paint/layer.js : the paint substrate's surface.  Plan: reality/art/onchain/alldogs/design/Paint_Substrate_Plan_20260904.html (section 2).
// One layer per painting.  Materials in src/paint/ act on it physically (deposit, pick up, read the surface); the 2D canvas is written
// once at the end.  The words and scenes do not know it exists: the material entry points route here when PK.kit.paint is set.
//
//   PK.paintBegin(ctx, rng, opts) -> layer     allocate at device resolution; the canvas as drawn so far (the ground) becomes the surface
//                                              colour; tooth (the canvas weave height) is made from an aperiodic noise field.
//       opts.tooth      rms height of the weave in paint units (0.02; one full loaded deposit is about 1.0)
//       opts.toothCell  grain cell of the weave in device px (2.6; the model is PK.paint.toothField in src/paint/ground.js)
//       opts.wetLife    strokes a deposit stays movable, e-fold (40)
//       opts.light      raking light angle, radians, direction the light comes FROM (-2.2 = upper left)
//       opts.elev       light elevation 0..1 (0.25), opts.shade diffuse strength (0.85, in linear light), opts.spec specular strength
//                       (0.06, linear light, times the cell's gloss), opts.blur passes (1), opts.finish the bare ground's gloss (0.05)
//       opts.photoDry   paintEnd photographs the painting dry (true): no wet sheen in the final composite
//       opts.grain      the weave as colour grain in the composite (0.025; round 5): diffuse x (1 + grain x tooth / rms tooth / (1 + height^2)).
//                       0 = the composite before round 5 (paint_composite_grain's planted negative).  See GRAIN in paintComposite
//       opts.finishFromHeight   the law before round 3 (gloss = min(1, 0.6 hgt + 0.8 wet), no finish channel): planted negative of
//                       rules/planted/paint_finish.js, never on in a painting
//       opts.lightByHeight  (round 6, P6 step 2) false: every film's relief lit in full, the law before round 6 (paint_light_by_height's
//                       planted negative).  opts.lightH0, opts.lightH1 override LIGHT_H0 / LIGHT_H1: the film (L.top, what the mark's own
//                       gesture laid at the cell) under which a mark composites matte, over which its relief is lit whole.  See paintComposite
//   FINISH (P1d round 3, Astra 4).  Gloss is a MATERIAL STATE, not a function of thickness: dry acrylic is matte to satin, house paint is
//   flat, wet paint and oil stick are glossy.  The layer carries fin (Float32 w*h, 0..1 gloss of what is on top); depositAt takes the paint's
//   finish and blends it in by the deposit's coverage; wet stock adds gloss up to WET_GLOSS (0.6) by min(1, wet) and so decays with the
//   wetness; paintComposite's specular lobe is opts.spec x gloss x (n.h)^24.  Before this a thick black body read dark grey (every thick
//   mark advertised a lit strip) and a thin wet stroke had no sheen.
//   LINEAR LIGHT.  The composite decodes col from sRGB, shades and adds the specular in linear light, encodes back.  The diffuse term
//   m = 1 + shade x (n.l - lz) is 1 on a flat surface, so a flat colour composites to itself (black stays black, 1/255); shade 0.85 in linear
//   gives the same lit +0.05 / shadow -0.07 on a 0.75 body the old 0.4 gave in encoded space, and less on a dark body, which is what the
//   eye sees.
//   P4 calibration (2026-09-04, box): bare cream ground composited, 240x240 window: grain sd 0.0047, lag-1 0.64, no spectral peak (1.2x),
//   features 1.8 x 1.4 px; the K 6 / tooth 0.18 / cell 2.2 / shade 0.22 / elev 0.55 stucco of the first smoke read sd 0.015.  Synthetic fat
//   stroke (60 px, hgt 1, lip 1.4): lit edge +0.050, shadow edge -0.071 of luminance against the body; a flat hgt-1 field sd 0.0002.
//   Round 3 (linear light, shade 0.85): the same stroke lit +0.046, shadow -0.074, flat field sd 0.0001; bare cream grain sd 0.0044.
//   Controls: rules/planted/paint_ground_bare.js, paint_light_ridge.js, paint_field_lanes.js.
//   PK.kit.paint                                the layer: { w, h, sx, sy, col (Float32 w*h*3, sRGB 0..1), hgt, wet0, wetT, tooth, fin, top, age, opts, laid, taken }
//                                              (top: the height the cell's most recent gesture laid there, reset when a later gesture first
//                                              deposits into the cell; the level passes and pickups leave it: it is the mark's film, not the pile)
//   LEDGER (round 4, P1e step 3): L.laid is every unit of height a deposit has put on the layer, L.taken every unit a pickup has taken off it;
//   the level passes move height and lose none (LEVEL_CONSERVE), so sum(hgt) - sum(hgt at paintBegin) = laid - taken at all times.  A brush
//   that deleted paint (the LEVEL loss before round 4) broke the ledger by 0.7 of every wet overlap; paint_merge_seam's CONSERVE row reads it.
//   FLOW_COL and HOLES (round 4, P1e step 3, in L.level): the paint the level passes move carries its colour and covers what it flows over
//   (a cell filled to the body's height by the body's paint reads the body's colour, not the pale of the thin film that was there), and a dry
//   cell with HOLE_N of its 8 neighbours wet, when those hold a loaded film (HOLE_W), is a hole the film closes over; the 1 px channel between
//   two dry-brush streaks (6 wet neighbours) and a 2x2 skip (5) stand.
//   PK.paintEnd(ctx)                            composite: colour lit by the height field (hgt + tooth showing where paint is thin), one
//                                              putImageData.  The layer stays for reading.  Calling it twice re-composites (idempotent).
//                                              The photograph is of the DRY painting (opts.photoDry, true): wet stock adds no gloss here;
//                                              PK.paintComposite(L, true) alone is the surface as it stands now, wet sheen and all.
//   PK.paintSync(ctx, fn)                       for a legacy material: write the unlit colour to ctx, run fn(ctx), read the ctx back into col.
//                                              hgt / wet untouched.  Slow (two full copies); use only for materials not yet on the substrate.
//   layer.tick()                                one stroke has ended: age++.  Every material calls it once per gesture.
//   layer.surfaceAt(X, Y)                       contact height at device cell = hgt + tooth * toothVisible(hgt)   (paint fills the weave)
//   layer.wetAt(X, Y)                           movable paint now (lazy decay from the stroke it was laid: wet0 * exp(-(age - wetT) / wetLife))
//   layer.depositAt(X, Y, r, g, b, amount, thick, wetness, glaze, finish, area)
//                                              lay paint: coverage a = area x (1 - exp(-amount * COVER)); hgt += amount x area x thick; fin = lerp(fin, finish, a)
//                                              (area: the share of the cell the film covers, 1 when absent; amount is the film's depth over
//                                              that share.  A half-covered cell is half paint and half what was under it, not a full cell
//                                              at half the optical depth: at amount 2.2 the old form read 0.91 covered for a 0.5 share,
//                                              this reads 0.50.  The brush sums its taps' shares per cell over a stroke and resolves once)
//                                              (finish: the paint's dry gloss 0..1; undefined = FINISH_DRY 0.15, matte acrylic); the colour by the film:
//                                              a body (glaze falsy, the default: every material's paint, a spray's dot at thick 0 too) covers,
//                                              col = lerp(col, c, a); a GLAZE (glaze true: the brush says so when its medium is thin, o.thick x
//                                              alpha under GLAZE, 0.4; a body dragged thin is not a glaze) is a transparent film,
//                                              col = col x (1 - ag + ag c) with ag = 1 - exp(-amount x thick x COVER), the pigment dilute
