//              (PUSH, round 4: a 40 px pair 30 px apart reads a smooth swell); the bead that stood was the one the next stroke's EDGE landed
//              on, under the soft fringe or a px past the outermost hair, because PUSH weighed a cell's excess by the hair's contact and the
//              fringe hairs (contact 0) passed over it and left it under a thin film (the pair 36 px apart: the covered bead stood 2.35 over
//              a 1.54 valley beside it, body 2.1; 38 px apart 2.7 over 1.06).  Now the contact weight is max(contact / DEAD, excess over
//              the face / SLUMP_H): a wet pile standing half a unit over the face is taken whole by any hair that covers it; and the cells
