//
//   PK.hand.pack(rng, frame, o) -> items            also the hand word h.pack(frame, o).  frame = [x0, y0, w, h] | {x, y, w, h} | {w, h}.
//     items: [{ type, cx, cy, r, z, id, seed, band, protect, dark, fill, ...band.props }] in PAINT ORDER (back to front), with items.report.
//     Sizes in px; the defaults below are Murakami's picture at U = min(w, h), written as fractions of U so any frame gets the same picture.
//     bands      [{ count, min, max, type | types, protect, props }]   scale bands, element RADIUS min..max px (or minFaceR..maxFaceR, the FACE disc's
//                radius, M01d's slot form: r = faceR / face), `count` of them; type is a
//                painter name ('flower', 'skull', 'paw'...) or types = { name: weight }; protect true = this band's face discs are protected;
//                props are copied onto every item of the band.  Default: M01c's census of the reference (17 large protected flowers,
//                59 + 125 + 186 flowers in three smaller bands, 160 skulls half small), radii from face radius / 0.48.
//     face       0.48   the protected disc's radius as a share of r (a flower's face disc)
//     protect    0.15   no LATER element may cover more than this share of a protected face disc (union, measured by 100 sample points)
//     protectBody 0.5   nor more than this share of a protected element's whole disc (its petals stay mostly visible)
//     front      false  true = protected elements are painted LAST (M01c's rule: they cover, nothing covers them); the placement then only
//                avoids burying others under them
//     core       0.78   the share of r an element is trusted to cover (petals reach r; the distance field uses core x r)
//     gap        px     stop filling when no gap wider than this remains (diameter; 0.0026 U = 2 px at 781)
//     fill       { type 'flower', min 0.128 U, max 0.154 U, props }   the gap fillers, painted at the BACK; false = none
//     maxCount   650    hard stop on the count (fillers included)
//     candidates 300    best-of-n candidate placement on the distance field (blue noise: the emptiest cell wins, jittered by r x jitter 0.32)
//     inset      0.8    a protected element's centre stays r x inset inside the frame
//     crowd      5      soft penalty per px a candidate overlaps a protected element's body (keeps the field clear round the big faces)
//     clusters   { n 26, size [3, 8], minR 0.0295 U, spacing 0.147 U, key 'dark' }   style clustering: n groups of size neighbouring
//                elements (larger than minR, group centres at least spacing apart) get item[key] = true; false = none.  A painter reads
//                item.dark and chooses its dark styles (the icons do).  Measured by PK.hand.packStats.clustering.
//     depthJitter 0.032 U   paint order: fillers, then the rest large-to-small with this jitter (small ones scattered over large ones)
//     anchors    [{ cx, cy, r, type, protect, ...props }]   placed first, exactly (a traced composition); the bands fill the rest
